#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/id #uuid "032ead48-0a3f-5a5e-b604-2a2fc0d91770" :question/math-academy-id "e-2288" :question/problem "The tape diagram below shows the ratio between small and big tokens in a desk game. What is the ratio of big tokens to all tokens?\n\n![](images/5b/5b779b66fb6e6717e102398153f09f3cb70582a4333a68ad2aeeb97fced47c9b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram for big tokens shows $4$ boxes. So, there are $4$ big tokens.\n\nAltogether, there are $12+4=16$ boxes. So, there are $16$ tokens in all.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of big tokens to all tokens is $4:16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ef376fd-9191-586d-b172-5e46e3043243" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Tape Diagrams Given a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "fe68a823-4477-5d82-bd17-12842d6e8735" :question/math-academy-id "e-2290" :question/problem "Abbie and Kate are making cupcakes. Abbie makes $5$ cupcakes for every $7$ that Kate makes. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that:\n\nAbbie makes $\\color{blue}5$ cupcakes for every $\\color{red}7$ that Kate makes.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Abbie's tape must contain $\\color{blue}5$ boxes, while Kate's tape should have $\\color{red}7$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/47/47c6e186cd17bffc7e83cca0c228bc1d05287cfba1bdb394c0a5dd71d411294a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073574 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/id #uuid "c089129a-f06b-53d3-a7be-d8d8a79b6dd9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2295" :question/problem "The tape diagram below shows the ratio between the number of orange plastic building blocks and blue plastic building blocks that Tom has. If there are $54$ orange plastic building blocks, how many plastic building blocks are there altogether?\n\n![](images/8c/8c05c3e85b33f385b2f4be02d57d1d34fdfcd94a6ca61b44411859d188f3d2cc.png)" :question/worked-solution "We are told that there are $54$ orange plastic building blocks. The tape diagram for orange plastic building blocks shows $6$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $54 \\div 6 = 9$ plastic building blocks.\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/16/16c543fb48a3d3c89c36b969cd4fceec36dd0c880664fd979c76740fd12c5722.png)\n\nSince there are $10$ boxes corresponding to the plastic building blocks in total, and each box represents $9$ plastic building blocks, the total number of plastic building blocks is:\n\n$$\n10 \\times 9 = 90\n$$\n\nSo, there are $90$ plastic building blocks."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76a2f388-bfe6-567b-beec-c59644da1e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/id #uuid "ca5d9154-4c7e-5866-a6eb-5e4c1fb4d24b" :question/math-academy-id "e-2296" :question/problem "A jar contains $60$ raffle tickets. The ratio of winning tickets to nonwinning tickets is shown in the diagram above. How many nonwinning tickets are in the jar?\n\n![](images/8b/8bdce5e82b4bcda74730503edebb9816d66175a1324784b11b9b08eeb17c9ba9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram shows $1$ box corresponding to winning tickets, and $4$ boxes corresponding to nonwinning tickets. Therefore, the ratio of winning to nonwinning tickets is $1:4.$\n\nWe are told that there are $60$ tickets in total. The tape diagram has $1+4=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $60 \\div 5 = 12$ tickets.\n\nNow, we fill the number $12$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/16/1669ac0d1aa6edd5bf53609121080dc8e8b685b57daa60b91daf3db816474ef2.png)\n\nSince there are $4$ boxes corresponding to nonwinning tickets, and each box represents $12$ tickets, the number of nonwinning tickets must be:\n\n$$\n4 \\times 12 = 48.\n$$\n\nSo, there are $48$ nonwinning tickets in the jar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0981974b-4b11-562e-8269-4a01f327a346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499675} {:answer/id #uuid "58068e59-01c8-54bb-9e62-077591373049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499824} {:answer/id #uuid "a79790f7-9e94-53c8-bad4-d716c82c0a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499979} {:answer/id #uuid "e0af79cf-8a55-522d-9a1a-07412a6e46af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500120} {:answer/id #uuid "e423cd67-ef0f-5d06-bf34-9c11e49a4c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58068e59-01c8-54bb-9e62-077591373049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499824} :answer-field/id #uuid "7257c5d5-ea4e-53c4-8793-0ce6c285b8ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0eac2215-e323-598c-aeac-4408994fc7bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-349283" :question/problem "![](images/55/556822d04577fef44f422814f5880fb885602bd6ea597f178b33df6bda4e11ba.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between red and blue marbles in Noah's collection. What is the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles?" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram for red marbles shows $3$ boxes while the tape for blue marbles contains $6$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is $3:6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "659816b1-cd37-5566-a7b1-ae62d4d67f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499852} {:answer/id #uuid "a9479b4c-abf3-5059-8fbe-45bb9b62f1a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8:13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499985} {:answer/id #uuid "b7188e03-4585-584a-9115-5dccb92fdfc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500026} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9acb24-baa7-5db2-bbbe-928834e7dd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500145} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ce9013-b1c4-564f-a661-79cf12f38fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "659816b1-cd37-5566-a7b1-ae62d4d67f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499852} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9269f1-c950-5d8b-b1a3-cf8c77135739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c899bac6-ef39-565f-bca3-4cc3481908c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-349287" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fac768ca9a6b8bd086b6dd9e44f6b564845bad8cae8a3d1345332f25d5cc3f4c.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between fiction and nonfiction books in a classroom library. What is the ratio of fiction books to all books?" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram for fiction books shows $5$ boxes while the tape diagram has $5+8=13$ boxes in total.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of fiction books to all books is $5:13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ef376fd-9191-586d-b172-5e46e3043243" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Tape Diagrams Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a2f1b6c-7f1a-52a6-b63f-38c2c15a8048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/31/315542297953311a7ebb8fe1ec63b6f896e0b06a526d49c0accac0837cfb9898.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499708} {:answer/id #uuid "2a501429-b6ac-5b92-a773-a758e7fc346a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a5d135c1b5694b7df7d82e83394aaf16bced84f701d83f9b0afbab11a442d699.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499744} {:answer/id #uuid "8448f8e8-4904-55b3-bddc-038681b853bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/64/64122b2cc13f0f0407e4be2c9aaec498617f2664ad4697cc6afcb413906a5b09.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499906} {:answer/id #uuid "86608a97-9087-54dd-b100-aac9a9d5fc62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bb22cee39c546443ad97504248d782df0785215bd86799818442c9cb9f6d29d9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499915} {:answer/id #uuid "a9098e3f-b50a-51eb-89bb-fb383cb7972b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28e279f136e9fe3c2db94f5897ad7de65f54dbb90368f0b172241264823a4151.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a2f1b6c-7f1a-52a6-b63f-38c2c15a8048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/31/315542297953311a7ebb8fe1ec63b6f896e0b06a526d49c0accac0837cfb9898.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499708} :answer-field/id #uuid "532e0590-e350-544a-9795-f9dcfa6ae770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc35b4b8-7e0d-5fe0-bbed-0dea389c7b90" :question/math-academy-id "q-349298" :question/problem "In one minute, Ava can type $3$ words while Ben types $5$ words. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that:  \n\nIn one minute, Ava can type $3$ words while Ben types $5$ words.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Ava's tape must contain $3$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to Ben should have $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/31/315542297953311a7ebb8fe1ec63b6f896e0b06a526d49c0accac0837cfb9898.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76a2f388-bfe6-567b-beec-c59644da1e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2666953e-f565-501b-94a6-cb52432ad99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499739} {:answer/id #uuid "38cc2aa5-4203-5da7-80a7-dba619f32a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499770} {:answer/id #uuid "3d54ec54-eb0c-559a-93fb-48d14fbd973e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499774} {:answer/id #uuid "b56c86de-3485-5e21-932e-a0931dc5e38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500022} {:answer/id #uuid "efea3a2d-be51-5fb2-a6b0-f017ef125038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efea3a2d-be51-5fb2-a6b0-f017ef125038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500149} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb295803-371c-5d9e-af5b-4a4e5e12624f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73f7645f-5556-5602-99d1-a98b9d1aa7ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-349312" :question/problem "![](images/ea/ea20fd21d0d8924163615500ebf0c5aaa1823a68121c0fc574624dfd8182fbf6.png)\n\nA box contains $25$ colored pencils. The ratio of red pencils to blue pencils is shown in the diagram above. How many blue pencils are in the box?" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram shows $3$ boxes corresponding to red pencils, and $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils. Therefore, the ratio of red to blue pencils is $3:2.$\n\nWe are told that there are $25$ pencils in total. The tape diagram has $3+2=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $25÷5=5$ pencils.\n\nNow, we fill the number $5$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/58/58a4e9ce8130b4e84307652c4237e0d898cfb56a9f25ab00669d376b3bfb4515.png)\n\nSince there are $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils, and each box represents $5$ pencils, the number of blue pencils must be:\n\n$$\n2\\times 5=10\n$$\n\nSo, there are $10$ blue pencils in the box."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76a2f388-bfe6-567b-beec-c59644da1e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef40008-17cc-5d46-9276-1a20bd40b1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499723} {:answer/id #uuid "64f60689-b357-578d-8669-cd5699f8108e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499850} {:answer/id #uuid "783751a9-a432-53e9-8bd7-8a03d54a5882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499876} {:answer/id #uuid "dab43930-651b-58b0-8ae4-b9c37c9494a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500103} {:answer/id #uuid "ef698e71-aced-5a26-a4cf-9c125a272cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "783751a9-a432-53e9-8bd7-8a03d54a5882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499876} :answer-field/id #uuid "295eea8d-3042-5402-89d4-b8c01da0cfbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05816576-2c37-58bb-af9f-d158df6b7282" :question/math-academy-id "q-349315" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4335622f7505350155fd5c84ce1cbdbb6c4fba4570b8cf4a4cd8982403ffede.png)\n\nAn aquarium has $45$ fish. The ratio of goldfish to guppies is shown in the diagram above. How many guppies are in the aquarium?" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram shows $2$ boxes corresponding to goldfish, and $3$ boxes corresponding to guppies. Therefore, the ratio of goldfish to guppies is $2:3.$\n\nWe are told that there are $45$ fish in total. The tape diagram has $2+3=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $45÷5=9$ fish.\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/06/069481a1ab6b18ebe6bf20053b793c49b54c06352f3acfc218aae32e34cd8f50.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ boxes corresponding to guppies, and each box represents $9$ fish, the number of guppies must be:\n\n$$\n3\\times 9=27.\n$$\n\nSo, there are $27$ guppies in the aquarium."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a73ab4f-1541-5b4e-871d-7540a822b110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499883} {:answer/id #uuid "98becb2c-eed8-5e52-8f23-258728c6306d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499951} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ec9381-9b95-53f2-8055-70a14b10b21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500030} {:answer/id #uuid "c009a2bc-53e0-58b5-9309-2182e8faddc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500045} {:answer/id #uuid "c5886644-6934-5a61-80fd-ca257c2f5e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98becb2c-eed8-5e52-8f23-258728c6306d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499951} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e07a1c-d165-5596-aedf-f135cce8a031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bb66df7-891d-5538-826d-40f885a0db34" :question/math-academy-id "q-61405" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a5fd1786ed953eec19da3c4f76f4b16e5d80db45bb0062d7690a665fe0f533d.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between correct and incorrect answers in Julia's math test. What is the ratio of incorrect answers to correct answers?" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram for incorrect answers shows $2$ boxes while the tape for correct answers contains $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of incorrect answers to correct answers is $2:5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222b2df1-cdfe-5720-b4fe-57977217ab0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499730} {:answer/id #uuid "2e55af62-7590-5a94-8c7e-d0aa4bc17e55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499752} {:answer/id #uuid "baa6ab20-8743-5e5a-9188-60328df8d713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500035} {:answer/id #uuid "de5d908a-8433-5374-9e03-478492b3a58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500112} {:answer/id #uuid "e00b9d89-e325-5b62-a4cd-e851429af6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baa6ab20-8743-5e5a-9188-60328df8d713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500035} :answer-field/id #uuid "a327ddaf-2ff0-5edf-a651-061132b049cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29d68311-d734-5664-956b-1dbe021c610a" :question/math-academy-id "q-61476" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e79f93d06560ea1a95116c0278e5536c4b629aa3ee04a24abc3c4a9f0f97b693.png)\n\nBarbie made a cake that had candied fruit and raisins. The ratio of candied fruit to raisins is given by the tape diagram above.  If she used $8$ ounces of candied fruit to make the cake, how many ounces of raisins did she use?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that Barbie used $8$ ounces of candied fruit in total. The tape diagram shows $4$ boxes for candied fruit. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $8÷4=2$ ounces.   \n\nNow, we fill the number $2$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/7c/7c40be92924cb2cebf8661802933280b59a843c3d0ab3616088c2a5643404449.png)\n\n \n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to raisins, and each box represents $2$ ounces, the number of ounces of raisins used was\n:\n\n$$\n5\\times 2=10\n$$\n\nSo, Barbie used $10$ ounces of raisins."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fc9a1b6-9c7b-59e1-81b7-9c5aa639433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499895} {:answer/id #uuid "ae83b0b4-4123-5cc1-9e33-357482fda453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500002} {:answer/id #uuid "b45c8010-7423-5107-8de6-af7542953589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500018} {:answer/id #uuid "cafbf5e3-c8e3-593f-9419-ee534075deed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500066} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a306e4-43ea-574e-b69e-98ea30a29631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b45c8010-7423-5107-8de6-af7542953589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500018} :answer-field/id #uuid "74f83c28-b548-59e6-b87c-e6a851d6f665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4c72bae-b132-52e1-8c37-a59f0f9c3c2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-61483" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c00fee9c5165bea605b349ee700e46c2e1898e7c6b65595c462207fd237d6e5a.png)\n\nSally made a necklace using cubic and spherical beads.  The ratio of cubic to spherical beads is given by the tape diagram above.  If there are $18$ spherical beads in the necklace, then how many cubic beads are there in total?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that there are $18$ spherical beads in total. The tape diagram for those shows $3$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $18÷3=6$ beads.  \n\nNow, we fill the number $6$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/9b/9b7efbe8e98fe498afbed34ffa33f02248eb72bd3a16a8683a5c26daefda9505.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to cubic beads, and each box represents $6$ beads, the number of the cubic beads is:\n\n$$\n5\\times 6=30\n$$\n\nSo, there are $30$ cubic beads in the necklace."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354ac960-677f-551a-9ce9-2a96a291649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499764} {:answer/id #uuid "6e54e3f8-576d-588f-9143-88e8b89aa3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499861} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7efe48-417e-5b36-85c8-80c25e17af61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499889} {:answer/id #uuid "84ce9ec7-b9f1-5dbb-a76c-e72a04efe5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499909} {:answer/id #uuid "d699150e-5a62-5ce4-8b68-529fd7c62a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84ce9ec7-b9f1-5dbb-a76c-e72a04efe5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0594b8e2-931c-592c-8dc4-588f0e38cb85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2d3a89a-3b53-50ea-ab1b-27e8bcd50832" :question/math-academy-id "q-61523" :question/problem "![](images/03/03b73d8213a55e4a50885b80b8f031de3186e46d9b358be792c2043b1c8a97b8.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between the number of liters of milk and juice that Bob buys in a month. If he buys $16$ liters of milk in a month, how many liters of milk and juice does he buy altogether?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that he buys $16$ liters of milk. The tape diagram for liters of milk shows $4$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $16÷4=4$ liters.\n\nNow, we fill the number $4$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/c8/c896618aebed4174005a7d47059eb74e24bc762645b8a46303a07e643c293407.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to the liters of juice and milk in total, and each box represents $4$ liters, the total number of liters is:\n\n$$\n4\\times 6=24\n$$\n\nSo, he buys $24$ liters of milk and juice altogether."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0583df89-041e-5716-af95-ad0c9e34690a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499662} {:answer/id #uuid "1817bc92-459c-5fcd-8cbb-98ffaa0ead78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499706} {:answer/id #uuid "30524095-39a7-50b4-917d-049f5b85fd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499757} {:answer/id #uuid "c766dc2f-41ae-5381-a852-34b3054afd50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500062} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4afc5a-0150-5a11-9740-d784a47099cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0583df89-041e-5716-af95-ad0c9e34690a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499662} :answer-field/id #uuid "37db5ec2-f9a8-5671-bc92-006c4e342a3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53afd0b5-618f-512e-b769-550096e6ab34" :question/math-academy-id "q-61532" :question/problem "![](images/38/3887946edaafb7d94bbf911c53cf1a0d2a48d43880829ce6069cc42d26eba526.png)\n\nTimmy set up a one-day lemonade sale in front of his house.  The ratio of disposable cups to lemonade servings is given by the tape diagram above. If he had a total of $40$ disposable cups to begin with, how many lemonade servings did he have then?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that there were $40$ disposable cups in total. The tape diagram for those shows $5$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $40÷5=8$ disposable cups.   \n\nNow, we fill the number $8$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/b3/b3ed4d72509ba29446f6da8919d81b4cce2dc57d6b80c8496f832c2ec5e95616.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to lemonade servings, and each box represents $8$ servings, the number of servings was:\n\n$$\n6\\times 8=48\n$$\n\nSo, Timmy had $48$ lemonade servings in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ef376fd-9191-586d-b172-5e46e3043243" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Tape Diagrams Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35cf29ef-fa27-5b6a-ad0c-dce433d96b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/97ec8d41ba37377fa508b26ea9cc0e370a971f9c124327772625d714477e7713.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499766} {:answer/id #uuid "7c439235-775c-5a1c-bd39-8f43d4d3ed93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d77a9e1a41ccf21f16cdc0ddb379f4fc436208571ceecdcea0a6f1ae494e76d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499888} {:answer/id #uuid "8b541712-d8e7-5ff4-80ad-e32b503f1e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/290ed3e67984cefd45affab89efb929baff403ba762885551a1ca4eb3d61e7ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499926} {:answer/id #uuid "d373d0b5-95ef-506e-bde7-ace6cdaa585d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f5c6a93a70f2bec8a304771af5cf5e09800bd53066bb351c92054ec2cc293b57.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500088} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c08a75-aa0a-5530-a4e5-fea2f73852b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ce/ce41ab7a0d8a4b0c426889fd1ae384e252b1490ee4a84e8fddc8cb27d54d467f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b541712-d8e7-5ff4-80ad-e32b503f1e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/290ed3e67984cefd45affab89efb929baff403ba762885551a1ca4eb3d61e7ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499926} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d623c64-3477-58d4-a5ef-1e0d40971801" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0da3c985-9149-5021-920d-90e4d419fc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-61538" :question/problem "Danny and Sheilah are making donuts. Danny makes $4$ donuts for every $5$ donuts Sheilah makes. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that:\n\nDanny makes $4$ donuts for every $5$ donuts Sheilah makes.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Danny's tape must contain $4$ boxes, while the tape corresponding to Sheilah should have $5$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/29/290ed3e67984cefd45affab89efb929baff403ba762885551a1ca4eb3d61e7ab.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b8c0741-12e8-5607-9251-e490c6eba03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073107} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a392ec-4cee-5871-b6fc-6331ca4b7b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073108} {:answer/id #uuid "da86c379-013c-5779-b1ce-6034a22fb1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073109} {:answer/id #uuid "edb37942-1add-5c46-88ee-533e60004d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073110} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6cf666-f42f-53f7-b789-37894a016423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da86c379-013c-5779-b1ce-6034a22fb1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073109} :answer-field/id #uuid "947bfb76-0df8-5831-900c-721df753ad3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "530832e4-8c4e-56d8-914c-0cc3fc44688c" :question/math-academy-id "q-61551" :question/problem "![](images/be/bed03c82d1116315a6841eee13cf3ed2c8011ff5992d9b36f2f3b9dbfe43bc84.png)\n\nThe tape diagram above shows the ratio between the number of stairs and carts in a warehouse. If there are $45$ stairs, how many stairs and carts are there in the warehouse altogether?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that there are $45$ stairs in the warehouse. The tape diagram for the stairs shows $5$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $45÷5=9.$\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/db/db352d53c2926e7a42b8183088a35860f057f4e5a845554ada955303e3dc8926.png)\n\nSince there are $9$ boxes corresponding to the stairs and carts in total, and each box represents $9$ of these items, the total number of stairs and carts are:\n\n$$\n9\\times 9=81\n$$\n\nSo, there are $81$ stairs and carts altogether."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1c04286-ecf9-5d7c-8cb5-a29a06933ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/